WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.860
Statues of heroes, foreboding hints at&nbsp;
the future, and blasts from the past.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:09.060
The new trailer for "The Mandalorian" is&nbsp;
filled with blink and you miss it details.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.800
With the "Star Wars" sequel trilogy wrapping up,&nbsp;
Lucasfilm and Disney turned their attention to&nbsp;

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.060
streaming in 2019. They came out of the&nbsp;
gate swinging with the Disney+ exclusive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.680
"The Mandalorian," which swiftly took the&nbsp;
television world by storm. Not only were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.880
audiences fascinated by the mysterious&nbsp;
Mandalorian bounty hunter Din Djarin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.480
but they couldn't get enough of his&nbsp;
lovable sidekick Grogu. It only made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.480
sense that the following year, a&nbsp;
second batch of episodes arrived.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:39.000
For Season 2, series creator Jon Favreau went&nbsp;
above and beyond for "Star Wars" fans. Boba&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.820
Fett returned from the grave, Cobb Vanth jumped&nbsp;
from print to TV, and animated icon Ahsoka Tano&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:49.500
finally appeared in a live-action production. He&nbsp;
even snuck in Luke Skywalker for good measure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:53.880
The bar is set incredibly high for Season&nbsp;
3, and the creators of "The Mandalorian" are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.380
working overtime to keep viewers glued to their&nbsp;
screens. Following an intriguing first trailer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:04.200
a new one premiered on January 16, 2023. Here are&nbsp;
some of the small details you might have missed.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:08.880
A locale we get quite familiar with throughout&nbsp;
the first season of "The Mandalorian" is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.260
Nevarro. It serves as a refuge for bounty&nbsp;
hunters, thieves, and general miscreants.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.640
The town is riddled with run-down buildings&nbsp;
and takes on a generally gloomy appearance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:22.440
It improves in the second season, thanks in&nbsp;
large part to its magistrate, Greef Karga.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.280
Before Nevarro became a sprawling&nbsp;
metropolis-in-the-making, remnants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.560
of the Galactic Empire tore it up in pursuit&nbsp;
of Din Djarin and Grogu. Din and his allies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:35.460
did a great job running the Empire out of&nbsp;
town, with one character making the ultimate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:40.380
sacrifice. To save everyone in "Chapter 8:&nbsp;
Redemption," IG-11 used its self-destruct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:44.940
capability to annihilate the Imperial troops.&nbsp;
In the new trailer, it's clear that to honor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:49.140
the assassin droid's memory, Karga has&nbsp;
erected a statue of IG-11 in the square.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:54.120
But just because Nevarro is thriving doesn't mean&nbsp;
that the entire galaxy is. As the "Mandalorian"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:58.740
Season 3 teaser continues, we learn that there's&nbsp;
trouble on the horizon. Speaking to Din Djarin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:01.800
fan favorite Captain Carson&nbsp;
Teva has some ominous words.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.720
"There's something dangerous happening out there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:08.520
and by the time it becomes big enough&nbsp;
for you to act, it'll be too late."

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.660
What could the X-wing pilot be alluding&nbsp;
to? He's likely talking about the Imperial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.400
remnant. Between Moff Gideon's desire to&nbsp;
use Grogu for unspecified experiments to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.760
his development of the Darktroopers,&nbsp;
it's apparent there's still a lot to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.360
be worried about. And based on what the&nbsp;
"Star Wars" sequel trilogy revealed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:27.540
the rise of the First Order, the&nbsp;
introduction of Supreme Leader Snoke,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:32.700
and the return of Emperor Palpatine are close at&nbsp;
hand. Teva has every reason to be on his toes.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.680
Another potential reveal also occurred in the new&nbsp;
trailer. As we hear Carson Teva's bleak voiceover,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:41.760
we see an unknown character sitting on&nbsp;
a ship next to a droid. They seem to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:45.540
be on a planet dominated by large&nbsp;
buildings and blinding lights. At&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:49.020
first glance, this location looks&nbsp;
incredibly similar to Coruscant.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:52.860
Coruscant was a key location throughout&nbsp;
the prequel "Star Wars" trilogy. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:57.120
also featured quite prominently on multiple&nbsp;
animated shows, various books, video games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.080
and more. Most recently, it appeared&nbsp;
on "Andor," where Rebel leaders Mon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.820
Mothma and Luthen Rael work to undermine&nbsp;
the Empire from right under its nose.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:09.840
As Din Djarin attempts to reconnect with&nbsp;
his Mandalorian roots, it should come as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:13.740
no surprise that "The Mandalorian" Season&nbsp;
3 is set to include several more of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:18.420
mysterious warriors. Throughout the trailer,&nbsp;
we see a few unrecognizable Mandalorians and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:22.140
some we've seen before, such as Paz&nbsp;
Vizsla. The number of Mandalorians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:25.980
is rivaled only by the number of droids we&nbsp;
see, which range from your run-of-the-mill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:31.560
astromechs to protocol droids of varying color&nbsp;
and make. Even a few B1 battle droids show up.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:36.120
A handful of them can be seen in a shot that seems&nbsp;
to depict a bunch of droids hanging out in a bar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:41.460
or mechanic shop of some kind. These flimsy robots&nbsp;
were staples of the "Star Wars" prequel trilogy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:46.440
They were destroyed in droves by clones and&nbsp;
Jedi alike at the command of Separatist leaders.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:49.920
"The Mandalorian" Season 3&nbsp;
premieres on Disney+ on March 1st.

